# Blizzard globals the Retail client no longer has, for the Check-Repo.ps1 `removed-api` rule.
# One "<name> <Retail version that removed it>" per line, # comments, sorted ordinally. A read (luac -l GETGLOBAL)
# of a listed name in an addon file is an error: the call fails with "attempt to call a nil value", and inside a
# coroutine or pcall nobody sees it (docs/work/2026-10-08-getiteminfo-removed). Use the C_ namespace function.
#
# 12.1.5: the ten deprecation addons Blizzard_Deprecated{CurrencyScript,Glue,ItemScript,ItemSocketInfo,LFG,PetInfo,
# PvpScript,SoundScript,TradeInfo,WorldElapsedTimerTypes} are deleted (Gethe/wow-ui-source ptr2, 12.1.5.70077). Every
# global they assigned in 12.1.0 (live, 69933; only with the loadDeprecationFallbacks CVar on) is listed; none is
# defined anywhere else in the 12.1.5 source, and the API documentation lists each only under its C_ namespace.

